{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778900462,"nonce":"+RUVaaYeQGZOyhGOuDa6k/7CnmQ=","title":"Mandible rebuild hook dirties package lock","message":"## Problem\nThe built-in Mandible post-merge auth hook runs `npm install \u0026\u0026 npm run build`. After the React Flow graph phase 2 merge, that plain install mutates `package-lock.json` by materializing React peer dependencies (`react`, `react-dom`, `scheduler`) even though the app intentionally uses Preact compat aliases. A dirty protected checkout then blocks auth approvals.\n\n## Context\nThis recurred after auth request `8aeb146d-5207-4dfc-9244-429bda37889f`: the merge and rebuild succeeded, but the hook left `package-lock.json` dirty. Cleaning the file unblocked the immediate workflow, but the hook needs a durable fix.\n\n## Proposed Fix\nUpdate the built-in hook command to run npm install with legacy peer dependency behavior, and add a migration to update existing databases that already seeded the old hook command.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}